  "welcomeBonus": "Cashback worth Rp 3.000.000 after activation and first transaction.",
  "notes": [
    "Earning is per whole Rp 20.000 multiple (Rp 100.000 for reduced-rate transactions) of the rupiah amount billed.",
    "Overseas means a currency other than rupiah; exclusions and reduced rates take precedence over the overseas rate.",
    "Power Bills payments at PLN earn nothing, while Power Bills insurance earns the reduced rate.",
    "Converting a purchase to Power Installment or Power Buy deducts its points; add \"cicilan\" to the description to reflect it.",
    "QRIS, installments, and virtual account payments are recognised only when the description contains those words.",
    "A Livin'poin converts to one mile at all five partners: KrisFlyer, GarudaMiles, Asia Miles, ANA Mileage Club and AirAsia Rewards. The cardholder gave the partner list and the one-for-one ratio; the bank's page advertises \"1:1 Mileage Redemption\" without naming either, so PinterPoin and Tuwaga are what confirm them.",
    "The one-for-one rate covers the first 25.000 Livin'poin a month, counted across every airline together rather than per airline. Beyond that the rate drops to 3.000 Livin'poin for 1.000 miles at all five partners, so the points still move, at a third of the value. Both are applied to transfer estimates. The ceiling is shared, so an estimate showing one airline assumes nothing has gone to the others that month.",
    "Livin'poin are credited per purchase, so the app checks this card per purchase.",
    "A conversion needs 10.000 Livin'poin to open and moves in 1.000 from there, so a balance of 15.000 converts in full rather than leaving 5.000 behind. The entry records the floor and the step separately, which an earlier version could not: it carried 10.000 as the step alone and rounded every balance down to a multiple of it.",
    "AirAsia Rewards opens at 1.000 rather than 10.000, which is the one partner without the larger floor. That is from Tuwaga rather than the cardholder.",
    "Livin'poin expire two years after they are earned, given by the cardholder. The app does not expire points, so a balance it shows may include points the bank has already dropped.",
    "The card carries no annual fee, main or supplementary, while the holder is a Bank Mandiri Prioritas customer.",
    "Converting to Asia Miles was withdrawn for a time and restored on 18 June 2026. The withdrawal date was not published, so the entry offers Asia Miles throughout and overstates the gap.",
    "A transfer estimate applies the ceiling. It is spent in whole transfer steps, and since the step is 1.000 the 25.000 ceiling lands exactly on one, so nothing is lost to rounding at the ceiling itself."
  ],
